  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
# No rule for /assets/* or /fonts/*: a path there with no file is answered with the dashboard shell, which must not be
# kept. The build appends a cache rule for each file it has in those directories (asset-headers.ts).
# The price pages, which Workers Assets answers without the Worker: revalidated as every page is, and never transformed
# on the way, so Cloudflare adds nothing to them (its analytics beacon, which the CSP refuses; api/src/worker.ts does the
# same for the pages the Worker answers). Their Markdown twins and the site's text files say their character set.
/pricing
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform
/compare/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform
/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
/*.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
